  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partnership Fund: UK/Africa/India Trilateral Research, Entrepreneurship and Innovation Partnerships</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FCDO&#x2019;s East Africa, Southern Africa, and South and Southeast Asia Research and Innovation Hubs funded three pilot initiatives in Kenya, Tanzania, South Africa and India. The programme activities included the delivery of a student hackathon in Kenya, a two-week student exchange programme at the Indian Institute of Technology Madras (IIT Madras), and a faculty exchange workshop bringing together institutions and innovation agencies from Kenya, India, South Africa and Kenya. The project supported the convening of a multistakeholder group to progress discussions between South African and Indian experts on an Agri-incubator focussed on neglected and underutilised species (NUS) crops in South Africa. The primary purpose of the support is development and not UK benefit.</narrative>
  </description>
